      "conclusion": "All eight exact normalized current shapes are bounded over0<abs(epsilon)<=.001 by their analytic zero-limit/reference endpoints. Maximum unit-current component shift3.16e-7 at70GeV. The paired70GeV K shift is3.9e-9 relative, unresolved within quadrature error. Overall coupling/epsilon dependence cancels K; this is a current-domain qualification, not an acceptance extrapolation.",
      "continuous_interval_derivation": "For t=k\u00b2 increasing with epsilon\u00b2, (1+t)A\u00b2-(z+d)A+zd=0 gives dA/dt=-A\u00b2/sqrt((z-d)\u00b2-4tzd)<0. Therefore h=d/[cw\u00b2(A-d)] is monotone on0<|epsilon|<=.001, bounded exactly by its zero-limit and reference endpoints. Overall em_coefficient/epsilon cancels the matched K.",
      "normalized_current_interval_proof": "For normalized v(h)=(u+h*w)/||u+h*w||, the derivative of each component has numerator (w_i*A-u_i*B)+(w_i*B-u_i*C)*h, A=u.u,B=u.w,C=w.w. Its possible internal extrema were checked explicitly; none lies in any of the8closed h intervals. Endpoint component envelopes therefore bound the continuous epsilon domain, not just the sampled epsilon grid.",
